ment scenarios (e.g., urban, rural, indoor, mobile).\n\nDesign a dynamic retransmission-timer policy T = T(state) — where 'state' may include locally observable quantities such as past ACK round-trip times, recent loss/duplicate-ACK events, spreading factor, duty-cycle constraints, and coarse load indicators — with the following requirements:\n\n1. Trigger awareness: the policy must explicitly mitigate retransmissions whose triggering cause is a delayed or corrupted ACK rather than a lost uplink message, using empirically identifiable retransmission triggers.\n2. Hardware feasibility: the policy must be implementable on resource-constrained end-device hardware (limited RAM, no floating-point unit, limited energy budget) and produce decisions in real time.\n3. Modularity: the policy must function as a stand-alone retransmission mechanism, without requiring joint operation with channel coding or payload compression.\n4. Cross-scenario robustness: the policy must achieve, across heterogeneous deployment scenarios, a provable or empirically demonstrated improvement over any static choice of T in terms of expected number of redundant retransmissions per successfully delivered message, while keeping the message delivery probability and end-to-end latency at least as good as a tuned static baseline.\n\nProvide such a policy together with an analysis (or testbed-validated evaluation) establishing properties (1)–(4).","status_search_result":"A targeted search did not surface a published dynamic LoRa retransmission-timer policy that simultaneously satisfies all four requirements (empirically grounded trigger awareness, constrained-hardware implementation, modularity independent of joint channel coding/compression, and cross-scenario robustness). Subsequent literature on LoRaWAN ADR and reliability typically addresses adaptive data rate, ACK-less reliability, or joint coding schemes rather than a stand-alone dynamic retransmission timer of the form requested. The problem therefore appears to remain open.","status_evidence":[{"title":"A Survey on LoRa Networking (open issues on retransmission)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.10195","snippet":"Static retransmission policy degrades the network performance ... This explains the need for dynamic retransmission policies. A modular retransmission policy without any dependencies on other techniques is inevitable.","claim":"The need for a dynamic, modular retransmission policy on constrained LoRa hardware is identified as an open issue."}]},"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"755cda25-e9ca-4bd6-ad39-0e93c6a47fe0"}
